# Floors for scripts/go-skip-census.sh (#9052 item 4).
#
# These are MEASURED values, not targets. The census reds in BOTH directions:
# an increase is a subject the suite stopped examining while still printing
# `ok`; a decrease is good news that must be banked by tightening the floor,
# because a loose floor is exactly that much room for the next regression to
# hide in.
#
# Raising a floor is allowed. Raising it SILENTLY is not — say why in the
# commit message, the same rule the Rust ignored-cell census applies to a new
# `#[ignore]`.

# #10716 banks the drift from the original 365-site measurement: 9 additional
# privilege-absent sites need kernel/network capabilities, and 15 additional
# non-privilege sites are fixture, socket, or external-input gated. Since the
# issue's 386-site recount, three further non-privilege sites were added:
# the #10702 Unix-socket availability guard and two #10641 bridge-netfilter
# availability guards. These reasons describe real skip conditions; the
# census counts them rather than claiming those cells ran.
# The 2026-09-24 master recount adds four #10708 route-reader cells gated on
# netlink handle creation, link/route reads, or a usable main-table route.
# The 2026-09-26 recount banks seven environment-gated cells merged without a
# floor update (CI runs no tests): #11191 x3 (loopback/second-interface
# availability for monitor-interface RETH tests), #11116 x2 (sshd/ssh-keygen
# binaries for factory root-login precedence), #11202 x1 (unconfigured host
# interface for monitor-traffic scope), #11156 x1 (loopback for RA goodbye
# suppression). All gate on execution-environment availability.
# The current-tree recount supersedes the 400-site measurement above: 17
# privilege-absent, 4 privilege-present, and 32 other concrete skip sites are
# now present, for 453 total including unchanged unparsed. #12119 adds one
# memlock-gated BPF_PROG_TEST_RUN regression, raising other and total by one.
# Merge composition with #12125/#12126/#12127 (measured, not banked drift):
# +2 priv-absent from #12127 dhcp_vrf_backstop netns guards, +3 priv-absent
# from #12125 manager_link_refresh netns guards, +1 other from #12126 FRR
# vtysh-absence skip. #11417's own +1/+1 floor lines are subsumed by this
# recount (same FRR-absence site).
# The census at base 83b5c9553 measured 467 total, 76 privilege-absent, and
# 376 other sites, versus these prior floors at 460/71/374: unrelated
# pre-existing drift of +7/+5/+2. #12083 adds seven environment-gated skip
# sites in pkg/routing/tunnel_keepalive_vrf_12083_test.go: +7 total, +5
# privilege-absent, and +2 other. Bank each delta separately and preserve
# both attributions in the commit body.
# #16474 banks the drift measured at a12d4aca (2026-10-24) against the
# aff843a4ec floors above: total 474 -> 557, priv-absent 81 -> 103,
# priv-present 14 -> 18, other 378 -> 435, unparsed unchanged at 1. The
# raw census reads 558/104 because it counts, inside a string literal in
# pkg/nfqueue/measure_gate_16436_test.go, the `t.Skip("netns child
# completed")` text that cell asserts is ABSENT from harness_test.go --
# a quoted fixture, not a call site (see that file). The floors below
# bank the corrected 557/103; the census script now excludes skip calls
# inside string literals, so its raw count and the floors agree.
# Gross movement since aff843a4ec (multiset by file+message, net in
# parens): priv-absent +24/-1 (+23: netns/VRF/dummy-interface creation
# guards in daemon routing-instance, mgmt-VRF and RPM kernel cells,
# flowexport routemask netns, frrconf service-group/root fixtures,
# kea perms root-only arms, dhcp-keep-survival unshare probe, authz
# loopback refusal; -1 the nfqueue harness Skip-on-success removed by
# #16436, whose quoted mention is the false positive above). priv-
# present +5/-1 (+4: root-bypass directory-permission arms in authz,
# first-commit teardown, zeroize seal and primary-listener holder;
# -1 the same zeroize arm moved from pkg/grpcapi to pkg/factoryreset).
# other +66/-9 (+57: loopback/interface/tool/fixture-gated cells --
# IPv6/loopback absence, dash/VLAN host-interface absence, vtysh
# absence, /dev/full, /proc, symlink and immutable-bit availability,
# golden-regen opt-in, -short timing probes, and fixture-stale premise
# guards that skip only when the collision they exercise no longer
# occurs; -9 removed or relocated cells including the zeroize trio's
# move and stale unix-socket guards). Every added site gates on
# execution-environment availability or on its premise being
# exercisable; none was un-skipped here because the gating condition
# is real on the hosts that lack it -- banking with these reasons is
# the #16474 acceptance path, and CI now ratchets any NEXT skip.
