# Disposition of PR #17623 (issue #16557)'s snapshot addition: its `t.Skip` branch says the
# zzq17760/zzq8100 collision pair no longer collides, but that pair still
# folds to the same u32 ID (1679679597), pinned in pkg/config/zoneid_test.go.
# Replace the unreachable-currently `t.Skip` with `t.Fatal`; the cell runs
# against the same fixture, and future premise drift fails instead of hiding.
# The six retired other sites are: the former PR #17623 (issue #16557)
# z174/z214 snapshot premise; three FRR-bgpd-absence guards replaced by PR
# #17583's vtysh oracle; and two loopback monitor gates replaced by PR #17430.
# This is the file+message recount and each remaining PR's disposition is
# listed explicitly in this PR body.
# PR #18751 (issue #18719) +1 priv-absent in
# pkg/fabricsegment/sampler_linux_test.go: the ONE skip site of the
# fabric-segment kernel cells (an empty private netns with CAP_NET_ADMIN and
# CAP_NET_RAW unavailable). make test-fabricsegment-kernel forces those cells
# by name under unshare -rn with XPF_REQUIRE_NETNS=1, where the site fails
# instead. (origin/master already measures 652 against this 607 floor; this
# line adds only #18751's own +1.)
total        = 608

# Privilege-dependent, split by DIRECTION because that split is the finding:
# no single run examines both groups. Running the suite as root does not close
# the gap, it swaps which subjects go unexamined.
priv-absent  = 121
priv-present = 18

# Everything else: environment-, tool- and fixture-gated skips.
other        = 468

# Skips this census counted but could NOT classify: `t.SkipNow()` (no message
# by construction) and non-literal messages. Deliberately a REPORTED bucket
# with its own floor rather than a silent drop — a census that quietly shrinks
# its own population is blind exactly where somebody wrote something unusual,
# and "unusual" correlates with "worth looking at".
unparsed     = 1
